---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Colophon · uxward">
  <style>
    .build-row .src-quiet { color: var(--tertiary); font-style: italic; }

    .title-block { padding-top: var(--space-9); padding-bottom: var(--space-10); }
    .title-eyebrow { font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--fs-13); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-7); }
    .title { font-weight: 900; font-size: var(--fs-d7); line-height: 0.96; letter-spacing: -0.04em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0; }
    .title em { font-style: normal; }
    .opening { font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--fs-22); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); max-width: 64ch; margin: var(--space-7) 0 0; }

    .section { padding: var(--space-10) 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); }
    .section-eyebrow { font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--fs-13); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }
    .section-head { font-weight: 900; font-size: var(--fs-d2); line-height: 1.05; letter-spacing: -0.025em; color: var(--ink); margin: 0 0 var(--space-9) 0; max-width: 20ch; }
    .section-head em { font-style: normal; }

    .spec { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); }
    .spec-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr 280px; gap: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-6) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); align-items: baseline; }
    .spec-row .key { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-11); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--tertiary); }
    .spec-row .name { font-weight: 800; font-size: var(--fs-26); line-height: 1.2; color: var(--ink); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
    .spec-row .name.mono { font-weight: 700; font-size: var(--fs-22); }
    .spec-row .name .why { display: block; font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--fs-16); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); margin-top: var(--space-3); max-width: 520px; }
    .spec-row a.src { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-13); letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; text-align: right; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .spec-row a.src:hover { color: var(--signature); }

    .color-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); }
    .color-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 200px 1fr 120px; gap: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-5) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); align-items: center; }
    .swatch { width: 56px; height: 56px; border: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); }
    .color-row .token-name { font-weight: 800; font-size: var(--fs-22); line-height: 1.2; color: var(--ink); letter-spacing: -0.015em; }
    .color-row .role { font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--fs-16); line-height: 1.5; color: var(--body); max-width: 480px; }
    .color-row .hex { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-12); letter-spacing: 0.04em; color: var(--tertiary); text-align: right; }

    .build-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); }
    .build-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr 280px; gap: var(--space-7); padding: var(--space-5) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); align-items: baseline; }
    .build-row .key { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-11); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--tertiary); }
    .build-row .what { font-weight: 500; font-size: var(--fs-18); line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink); }
    .build-row .what em { font-style: italic; font-weight: 400; color: var(--body); }
    .build-row a.src { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-13); letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; text-align: right; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    .build-row a.src:hover { color: var(--signature); }

    .ack-prose p { font-weight: 400; font-size: var(--fs-18); line-height: 1.7; color: var(--body); max-width: 660px; margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); }
    .ack-prose p strong { font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
    .ack-prose p em { font-style: italic; }
    .ack-prose a { color: var(--ink); }
    .ack-prose a:hover { color: var(--signature); }

    .stamp-row { padding: var(--space-9) 0 var(--space-10); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--space-7); flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .stamp-row .stamp { font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--fs-11); letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--tertiary); }
    .stamp-row .fleuron { font-size: var(--fs-22); color: var(--tertiary); }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .spec-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .spec-row a.src { text-align: left; }
      .color-row { grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; }
      .color-row .role { display: none; }
      .build-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .build-row a.src { text-align: left; }
    }

    /* Cyber easter egg — the colophon documents a different system once the
       override fires. The .cyber class on <html> swaps which version shows. */
    .cyber-only { display: none; }
    :global(.cyber) .normal-only { display: none; }
    :global(.cyber) .cyber-only { display: block; }
    :global(.cyber) .title-block .title {
      font-family: var(--cf-head);
      font-variation-settings: normal;
      letter-spacing: 0;
      font-size: var(--fs-d4);
      line-height: 1.15;
      text-shadow: 0 0 6px #19F0FF, 0 0 16px rgba(255, 43, 214, 0.6);
    }
    :global(.cyber) .title-block .title em { font-variation-settings: normal; }
  </style>

  <div class="container title-block">
    <div class="normal-only">
      <div class="title-eyebrow">Colophon · How this was made</div>
      <h1 class="title">A note on the <em>making.</em></h1>
      <p class="opening">
        uxward.com is where I keep my work and my writing. It has a light mode and a dark mode
        (and a super-secret easter-egg mode), one typeface, and it gets revised when I get around to
        it. Most people will never see this page. If you're reading it: hi. I like you already.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="cyber-only">
      <div class="title-eyebrow">Colophon · Override engaged</div>
      <p class="title">A note on the <em>breach.</em></p>
      <p class="opening">
        You found the override. The same working journal, jacked into Night City: wet
        asphalt, fluorescent signage, and a handbrush face pulled off the shelf for the
        occasion. Type the code again, click the radiation symbol, or press Esc, to surface back into daylight.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Typography</div>
      <div class="normal-only">
        <h2 class="section-head">One typeface. <em>That's it.</em></h2>
        <div class="spec">
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="key">Everything</span>
            <span class="name">
              Archivo
              <span class="why">A grotesque by <a href="https://www.omnibus-type.com/fonts/archivo/" target="_blank">Omnibus Type</a>. It does everything here: headlines, body, labels, numbers. The site speaks in a single voice.</span>
            </span>
            <a class="src" href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Archivo" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Omnibus Type</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cyber-only">
        <h2 class="section-head">One face becomes <em>three, after dark.</em></h2>
        <div class="spec">
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="key">Override display</span>
            <span class="name">
              Rock Salt
              <span class="why">A weathered handbrush face by Sideshow. It stays asleep until you type the code, then it tags the wordmark and headlines like graffiti. You could never read a paragraph in it, and that's fine. It's only here to shout.</span>
            </span>
            <a class="src" href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Rock+Salt" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Sideshow</a>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="key">Everything legible</span>
            <span class="name">
              Orbitron
              <span class="why">The sci-fi face that handles body text in Night City. Archivo takes a nap until you come back up.</span>
            </span>
            <a class="src" href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Orbitron" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The League of Moveable Type</a>
          </div>
          <div class="spec-row">
            <span class="key">Nav & signage</span>
            <span class="name mono">
              Sixtyfour
              <span class="why">A raster homage to the Commodore 64's own typeface, built for CRT scanlines. Runs the header, footer, and mobile-menu labels, signage that reads like an old terminal.</span>
            </span>
            <a class="src" href="https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Sixtyfour" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Jens Kutilek</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Color</div>
      <div class="normal-only">
        <h2 class="section-head">Five colors. <em>Only one of them is allowed to be loud.</em></h2>
        <div class="color-list">
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #E7E7E7;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Canvas</div>
            <div class="role">The page. Off-white on purpose; pure white is harsh on the eyes.</div>
            <div class="hex">#E7E7E7</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #FAF8F4;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Paper</div>
            <div class="role">A tinted surface for the few framed and inset moments.</div>
            <div class="hex">#FAF8F4</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #040404;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Ink</div>
            <div class="role">Headlines, wordmark, body text. Not quite black, for the same reason.</div>
            <div class="hex">#040404</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #646464;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Tertiary</div>
            <div class="role">Labels, timestamps, and the faint rules. Meant to stay out of the way.</div>
            <div class="hex">#646464</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #CC0006;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Signature red</div>
            <div class="role">The section numbers, the contact block, every link hover. It's the only color that gets to make noise, so it makes a lot of it.</div>
            <div class="hex">#CC0006</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cyber-only">
        <h2 class="section-head">More tokens, <em>and none of them rationed.</em></h2>
        <div class="color-list">
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #07060F;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Canvas</div>
            <div class="role">Almost black, with a little violet in it. Wet asphalt.</div>
            <div class="hex">#07060F</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #0E0B1D;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Paper</div>
            <div class="role">One step up from the background, for panels and callouts.</div>
            <div class="hex">#0E0B1D</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #F6F7FF;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Ink</div>
            <div class="role">Off-white text with a cyan glow.</div>
            <div class="hex">#F6F7FF</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #FF2BD6;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Neon pink</div>
            <div class="role">The signature red, after dark. Loudest sign on the street.</div>
            <div class="hex">#FF2BD6</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #19F0FF;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Neon cyan</div>
            <div class="role">The glow: reflections, selection, hover.</div>
            <div class="hex">#19F0FF</div>
          </div>
          <div class="color-row">
            <div class="swatch" style="background: #2B6BFF;"></div>
            <div class="token-name">Neon blue</div>
            <div class="role">The cool end of the palette. Rain and distance.</div>
            <div class="hex">#2B6BFF</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Build</div>
      <h2 class="section-head">What it's <em>built on.</em></h2>
      <div class="build-list">
        <div class="build-row">
          <span class="key">Night City</span>
          <span class="what">A second art direction, asleep until you type the word. <em>Five words wake it; one of them is a 1993 cheat code.</em></span>
          <span class="src src-quiet">undocumented</span>
        </div>
        <div class="build-row">
          <span class="key">Framework</span>
          <span class="what">Astro. <em>Plain HTML comes out the other end, which is all a site like this needs.</em></span>
          <a class="src" href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">astro.build</a>
        </div>
        <div class="build-row">
          <span class="key">Hosting</span>
          <span class="what">Cloudflare. <em>A minute to set up, seconds to connect to GitHub, minutes to deploy. Done.</em></span>
          <a class="src" href="https://www.cloudflare.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com</a>
        </div>
        <div class="build-row">
          <span class="key">Content</span>
          <span class="what">HTML. <em>Essays and case studies hand-authored in plain, portable markup I'll still be able to read in 2046.</em></span>
          <a class="src" href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">html.spec.whatwg.org</a>
        </div>
        <div class="build-row">
          <span class="key">Domain</span>
          <span class="what">uxward.com: <em>registered 2020, used in earnest 2026.</em></span>
          <span class="src"></span>
        </div>
        <div class="build-row">
          <span class="key">Source</span>
          <span class="what">Public on GitHub. <em>Go look; I built this too.</em></span>
          <a class="src" href="https://github.com/uxward/uxward" target="_blank" rel="noopener">/uxward/uxward</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Decisions</div>
      <h2 class="section-head">Things I decided, <em>and things I decided against.</em></h2>
      <div class="choices">
        <div class="choice-row">
          <div class="key">Chose to</div>
          <div class="val"><strong>Preach about stuff.</strong> My work, my experience, my opinions, etc. They're here. Have at them. Happy if you like them, it's okay if you don't.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="choice-row">
          <div class="key">Chose to</div>
          <div class="val"><strong>Wire the masthead to the repository.</strong> The four cells at the top of the home page report the last thing shipped, the last thing written, and the commit this build came from. None of it is typed by hand, so none of it can quietly go stale.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="choice-row">
          <div class="key">Chose to</div>
          <div class="val"><strong>Show 29 projects out of 100-plus.</strong> Not everything I've shipped is worth your time, and pretending otherwise would be its own kind of lie. So you get both numbers.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="choice-row">
          <div class="key">Chose <strong>not</strong> to</div>
          <div class="val"><strong>Put client logos on the site.</strong> A logo tells you who paid me, not what I did, and half this work is under NDA anyway. What actually happened is the credential.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="choice-row">
          <div class="key">Chose <strong>not</strong> to</div>
          <div class="val"><strong>Hide the parts that went wrong.</strong> Every case study here says what I'd do differently. Nobody's portfolio is actually mistake-free; the ones that look that way have just been edited.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="choice-row">
          <div class="key">Chose to</div>
          <div class="val"><strong>Give dark mode two reds.</strong> Red type on a dark page has to be lighter to stay legible; pale type on a red field needs that field to be darker. One value cannot do both, so the signature is two tokens after dark and one in daylight.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">✦ Informed by</div>
      <h2 class="section-head">Borrowed, <em>with thanks.</em></h2>
      <div class="ack-prose">
        <p>
          The grid-you-can-see comes from <strong><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wim_Crouwel" target="_blank">Wim Crouwel</a></strong>.
          The one-typeface rule comes from <strong><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Experimental_Jetset" target="_blank">Experimental Jetset</a></strong>.
          Black, white, and one loud color is <strong><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Massimo_Vignelli" target="_blank">Massimo Vignelli</a></strong>, by way of the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unigrids" target="_blank">Unigrid</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          And to the reader who got to the bottom of the colophon: <em>thank you for
          looking.</em> You are why the site is here. <a href="/ink">Here's something fun and beautiful, just for you.</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="stamp-row">
      <span class="stamp">Last revised Q2 2026 · Updated occasionally · Brandon E. B. Ward · Dallas</span>
      <span class="fleuron" aria-hidden="true">❦</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
